- 3.16.1 If two or more policies are taken by an insured during a period from one or more insurers, the contribution clause shall not be applicable for such policies where the cover/benefit offered: 

   - a. is fixed in nature; 

   - b. does not have any relation to the treatment costs; 

- 3.16.2 In case of multiple policies which provide fixed benefits, on happening the event in accordance with the terms and conditions of the policies, the insurer shall make the claim payments independent of payments received under other similar polices. 

- 3.16.3 If two or more policies are taken by an insured during a period from one or more insurers, where the purpose of such policies is to indemnify the treatment costs, the insurer shall not apply the contribution clause, but the policyholder shall have an 

option to chose insurer with whom the claim to be settled. In all such cases, the insurer shall be obliged to settle the claim without insisting for contribution clause.
